          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "spenden goes back to Middle High German spenden and Old High German spentōn \"to spend, to use\" (EtymDB). It is usually traced to Medieval Latin spendere, from expendere \"to weigh out, to pay out\" (Lewis & Short); English spend is a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
