              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "engagieren — \"to get involved (mostly reflexive, sich engagieren); to hire (an artist)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sie engagiert sich seit Jahren für den Tierschutz. She has been involved in animal protection for years."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mostly reflexive: sich für etwas engagieren. Said the French way: an-ga-ZHEE-ren. Einen Musiker engagieren — to hire a musician."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "engagieren was borrowed from French engager \"to pledge, to bind\" (EtymDB), built on gage \"a pledge\", which is usually traced to a Frankish word; EtymDB lists Old High German wetti \"a pledge, a security\" as a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
